1
00:00:01,353 --> 00:00:04,093
Previously on JoJo's Bizarre Adventure!

2
00:00:08,533 --> 00:00:09,513
What the?

3
00:00:09,673 --> 00:00:10,973
Why am I a kid?

4
00:00:11,953 --> 00:00:12,783
Tommy!

5
00:00:13,553 --> 00:00:15,853
Little boy, are you all right there?

6
00:00:16,153 --> 00:00:19,447
I'll clean those wounds up
and put some medicine on you.

7
00:00:24,753 --> 00:00:26,033
That's impossible!

8
00:00:27,213 --> 00:00:28,173
Chariot, help!

9
00:00:32,013 --> 00:00:33,093
Yes! Yes!

10
00:00:44,733 --> 00:00:47,321
I'm not strong enough
to beat him like this.

11
00:00:48,453 --> 00:00:50,653
I don't see that nice lady anywhere.

12
00:00:51,113 --> 00:00:52,073
Where'd she go?

13
00:00:52,373 --> 00:00:54,110
She couldn't have just vanished.

14
00:00:54,193 --> 00:00:55,830
She was sitting right behind me.

15
00:00:55,913 --> 00:00:57,733
I didn't even hear a scream.

16
00:00:58,013 --> 00:00:59,189
What'd he do to her?

17
00:01:01,393 --> 00:01:03,133
Where could she have gone?

18
00:01:03,333 --> 00:01:04,993
I'll pull the wrap.

19
00:01:07,033 --> 00:01:10,833
As I recall, you said the
shampoo stings your eyes.

20
00:01:10,953 --> 00:01:13,835
And since it looks like
you've got some in there.

21
00:01:17,773 --> 00:01:20,013
Allow me to help you wash it out!

22
00:01:20,413 --> 00:01:22,373
Now this won't take long.

23
00:01:32,153 --> 00:01:37,393
Gameta, uu, eucada, seaguretsho,
Saudi o na Mode Days?

24
00:01:38,133 --> 00:01:41,493
Mode, uu, eucanasu.

25
00:01:48,393 --> 00:01:51,573
Shultyaq no Chaka ga-su Cameo na hono,

26
00:01:52,393 --> 00:01:54,630
Omi-ki-o-se ra-leta,

27
00:02:13,813 --> 00:02:15,413
Stop, get down

28
00:03:02,033 --> 00:03:03,113
C 'est mauvais!

29
00:03:03,553 --> 00:03:06,650
Having bite-sized arms is gonna
wind up getting me killed!

30
00:03:06,733 --> 00:03:09,830
If only these stupid arms of
mine were just a little longer,

31
00:03:09,913 --> 00:03:13,148
I'd be able to poke his eyes
out and make a run for it!

32
00:03:15,893 --> 00:03:19,364
So, even in the face of death,
you've got to pull the plug.

33
00:03:20,593 --> 00:03:21,423
However...

34
00:03:26,353 --> 00:03:28,710
With your hair clogging
the water's only exit,

35
00:03:28,793 --> 00:03:31,690
it'll take even longer for
the tub to completely drain.

36
00:03:31,773 --> 00:03:34,655
I'd say you'll have five,
maybe ten minutes left.

37
00:03:37,653 --> 00:03:39,953
You may as well throw in the towel now!

38
00:03:40,733 --> 00:03:43,133
You're going down for a permanent nap!

39
00:03:43,353 --> 00:03:44,313
Good night!

40
00:03:44,613 --> 00:03:46,437
Horrid dreams, you little brat!

41
00:03:47,813 --> 00:03:48,793
I'll die!

42
00:03:50,773 --> 00:03:53,949
How does it feel knowing
that you're utterly helpless,

43
00:03:54,233 --> 00:03:55,063
Vulnerable!

44
00:04:00,813 --> 00:04:01,643
Hmm?

45
00:04:08,573 --> 00:04:10,253
What the hell is that thing?

46
00:04:11,373 --> 00:04:12,473
It can't be!

47
00:04:12,633 --> 00:04:14,750
But from the shape and
color, it looks like...

48
00:04:14,833 --> 00:04:15,853
There's no way!

49
00:04:16,053 --> 00:04:20,877
No one in their right mind would think of
doing something so downright disgusting!

50
00:04:25,873 --> 00:04:26,993
It's undeniable!

51
00:04:27,293 --> 00:04:28,633
The smell proves it!

52
00:04:29,373 --> 00:04:30,413
How foul!

53
00:04:30,773 --> 00:04:32,833
You took a shit in the bathtub!

54
00:04:37,153 --> 00:04:41,373
Guess I'm not so helpless after
all, you creepy four-eyed asshole!

55
00:04:41,693 --> 00:04:44,573
How dare you do something
like that? Dear God!

56
00:04:45,613 --> 00:04:48,510
Isn't there a shred of
human decency in your body?

57
00:04:48,593 --> 00:04:51,870
What kind of hero would ever stoop
to doing something so disturbing?

58
00:04:51,953 --> 00:04:53,873
You are a bad boy!

59
00:04:54,093 --> 00:04:55,013
Very bad!

60
00:04:55,373 --> 00:04:57,830
Shut up and tell me what
you did to that nice lady!

61
00:04:57,913 --> 00:04:59,384
I want to know right now!

62
00:04:59,993 --> 00:05:01,073
Where are you?

63
00:05:01,873 --> 00:05:02,793
Where'd you go?

64
00:05:03,213 --> 00:05:04,953
Lady, answer me!

65
00:05:06,013 --> 00:05:06,933
Hey, lady!

66
00:05:09,553 --> 00:05:11,713
Come on, you that stupid?

67
00:05:12,433 --> 00:05:15,493
What do you think I did? Whoa there!

68
00:05:15,913 --> 00:05:19,170
It'd be wise for both of us to
watch where we step, Polnareff.

69
00:05:19,253 --> 00:05:24,253
One wrong move and your lady friend is
likely to be squashed underfoot. Huh?

70
00:05:36,613 --> 00:05:38,073
He... he wouldn't.

71
00:05:38,493 --> 00:05:40,093
There's no way.

72
00:05:40,413 --> 00:05:41,873
This can't be happening.

73
00:05:44,973 --> 00:05:45,803
No!

74
00:05:45,953 --> 00:05:46,910
It can't be!

75
00:05:46,993 --> 00:05:49,670
Anyone who's unfortunate
enough to come into

76
00:05:49,753 --> 00:05:53,533
contact with my stand
experiences time in reverse.

77
00:05:53,913 --> 00:05:54,993
Luckily for you,

78
00:05:55,273 --> 00:05:58,650
you saw me coming and jumped away
from my shadow at the last second,

79
00:05:58,733 --> 00:06:01,510
buying yourself a few more years
than your friend down there.

80
00:06:01,593 --> 00:06:05,510
But she had the misfortune of touching
my shadow for several seconds,

81
00:06:05,593 --> 00:06:08,213
which is the reason she became a fetus!

82
00:06:10,793 --> 00:06:14,170
She's alive for the time being,
but if I'm being honest with you,

83
00:06:14,253 --> 00:06:17,782
she won't last long outside the
safety of her mother's womb.

84
00:06:18,913 --> 00:06:20,153
That's what she gets!

85
00:06:20,313 --> 00:06:23,590
She should have never tried to help
a pathetic piece of trash like you!

86
00:06:23,673 --> 00:06:25,073
What a moron!

87
00:06:27,653 --> 00:06:30,693
You are the worst kind
of person on this planet!

88
00:06:37,213 --> 00:06:40,153
Crap, you've got to be
kidding me! I just...

89
00:06:43,713 --> 00:06:45,948
Oops, looks like you touched it again.

90
00:06:46,113 --> 00:06:48,730
Which means you're going
to get even younger.

91
00:06:48,813 --> 00:06:49,653
This time,

92
00:06:49,753 --> 00:06:53,450
you'll probably regress to a diminutive
four-year-old version of yourself.

93
00:06:53,533 --> 00:06:54,363
Not again!

94
00:06:58,733 --> 00:06:59,813
This isn't good.

95
00:07:00,153 --> 00:07:02,153
I have to hurry and beat this guy.

96
00:07:02,353 --> 00:07:04,430
Or the nice lady will...

97
00:07:04,513 --> 00:07:08,450
At this rate, she only has a
matter of minutes before she dies!

98
00:07:08,533 --> 00:07:13,180
I've got to find a way to defeat this
Alessi freak, and I've got to do it fast!

99
00:07:16,873 --> 00:07:19,344
She took me in and fixed up all my wounds.

100
00:07:19,713 --> 00:07:20,873
She was so caring.

101
00:07:21,653 --> 00:07:22,913
I have to hurry.

102
00:07:23,273 --> 00:07:25,391
There's absolutely no time to waste.

103
00:07:30,113 --> 00:07:31,773
Get over here, will ya?

104
00:07:32,013 --> 00:07:34,170
Where exactly do you think you're going?

105
00:07:34,253 --> 00:07:36,690
You're not going to get
far cradling a dying fetus!

106
00:07:36,773 --> 00:07:38,573
Here's a fun idea.

107
00:07:38,933 --> 00:07:40,973
Let's turn you into a fetus!

108
00:07:42,533 --> 00:07:43,933
Dammit, not this again!

109
00:07:44,213 --> 00:07:46,213
His dumb shadow keeps touching me!

110
00:07:49,693 --> 00:07:52,013
Oh no, I'm getting even smaller!

111
00:07:53,093 --> 00:07:53,923
Yahoo!

112
00:07:54,006 --> 00:07:54,836
Oh boy!

113
00:07:55,013 --> 00:07:57,330
There's no way in hell I'm gonna lose now!

114
00:07:57,413 --> 00:08:01,410
Judging from your appearance, Polnareff,
you're what, three years old now?

115
00:08:01,493 --> 00:08:06,081
Before you know it, your intellect will
be that of a three-year-old's as well.

116
00:08:18,893 --> 00:08:21,893
Locking the door won't do
you any good, little one.

117
00:08:29,933 --> 00:08:30,763
Made it!

118
00:08:31,453 --> 00:08:34,277
Damn it, the stupid bars
are too close together!

119
00:08:34,913 --> 00:08:36,678
Even a kid can't slip through.

120
00:08:38,133 --> 00:08:42,790
But I have to find a way to get out of here
or that freak shoe's gonna kill us both!

121
00:08:42,873 --> 00:08:43,703
Crap!

122
00:08:46,413 --> 00:08:47,953
I, I can't cut them.

123
00:08:50,813 --> 00:08:52,813
This is just too crude to be true.

124
00:08:53,033 --> 00:08:55,690
I see that your chariot
has also become a toddler.

125
00:08:55,773 --> 00:08:58,313
The bars are too tough
for its baby rapier.

126
00:08:58,493 --> 00:09:00,199
I bet it's gotten slower too.

127
00:09:01,613 --> 00:09:04,473
Ready or not, here I come!

128
00:09:21,133 --> 00:09:24,593
Opal Neref, here comes Alessi!

129
00:09:32,353 --> 00:09:33,810
He's gone, huh?

130
00:09:33,893 --> 00:09:35,053
Where did he go?

131
00:09:35,293 --> 00:09:36,193
That brat!

132
00:09:36,613 --> 00:09:37,913
It just vanished!

133
00:09:38,393 --> 00:09:40,890
Or maybe the little
spunk monkey found a way

134
00:09:40,973 --> 00:09:43,444
to slither through the bars in the window!

135
00:09:47,153 --> 00:09:48,253
Clever, Bulnara.

136
00:09:48,453 --> 00:09:49,293
Very clever.

137
00:09:49,713 --> 00:09:52,360
You're trying to pull
a fast one, aren't you?

138
00:09:52,493 --> 00:09:55,730
You think if you trick me into believing
you slipped through the window,

139
00:09:55,813 --> 00:09:56,770
it'll distract me.

140
00:09:56,853 --> 00:10:00,382
You must be hiding somewhere,
waiting to get the drop on me.

141
00:10:01,673 --> 00:10:03,413
Not bad, runt.

142
00:10:03,973 --> 00:10:07,213
Quite cunning indeed for
a miserable little shit.

143
00:10:08,133 --> 00:10:10,957
Polnareff, come out, come
out, wherever you are.

144
00:10:12,433 --> 00:10:16,933
You're so puny now, you could easily
be hiding in that drawer over there.

145
00:10:17,393 --> 00:10:20,893
Yeah, he's probably hiding
in the bucket or the drawer.

146
00:10:21,253 --> 00:10:25,053
Or maybe he's actually hiding
in that teddy bear by the wall.

147
00:10:27,193 --> 00:10:28,653
Oh, where could he be?

148
00:10:28,933 --> 00:10:30,757
I've got a one in three chance.

149
00:10:31,013 --> 00:10:34,484
And if at all possible, I'd
like to get him with one swing.

150
00:10:34,593 --> 00:10:37,534
I'll crack open his infantile
skull with this axe!

151
00:10:42,693 --> 00:10:46,517
I've decided you're tucking away
in that tattered old teddy bear!

152
00:10:47,633 --> 00:10:53,813
But my second guess is this grandfather
clock, the perfect hiding spot for a coward!

153
00:10:57,413 --> 00:10:59,573
I guess I was wrong.

154
00:11:01,053 --> 00:11:03,190
Then maybe he's...

155
00:11:03,273 --> 00:11:05,313
Hiding in this rusty bucket!

156
00:11:06,233 --> 00:11:07,553
But I...

157
00:11:09,793 --> 00:11:11,933
So you are in the bear!

158
00:11:13,613 --> 00:11:15,233
Then how about the drawer?

159
00:11:17,313 --> 00:11:18,653
Where is he?

160
00:11:18,753 --> 00:11:20,330
Where is he? Where is he?

161
00:11:20,413 --> 00:11:21,243
Where is he?

162
00:11:21,326 --> 00:11:22,156
Where is he?

163
00:11:22,239 --> 00:11:23,069
Where is he?

164
00:11:23,533 --> 00:11:25,393
He's gone! But how?

165
00:11:25,793 --> 00:11:28,590
There's no way he could
have gotten out of here!

166
00:11:28,673 --> 00:11:31,261
The walls, floor, and
ceiling are all stone.

167
00:11:31,393 --> 00:11:34,630
Even if they were one centimeter
thick, Chariot couldn't break through.

168
00:11:34,713 --> 00:11:36,730
And those bars are too narrow for him.

169
00:11:36,813 --> 00:11:38,342
I saw it with my own eyes.

170
00:11:38,553 --> 00:11:40,693
This is insane. Where is he?

171
00:11:40,853 --> 00:11:41,953
Where did he go?

172
00:11:46,233 --> 00:11:49,690
So, you were outsmarted by
a toddler, huh? What the?

173
00:11:49,773 --> 00:11:52,413
Oh, man, Alessi.

174
00:12:01,993 --> 00:12:03,533
What's going on here?

175
00:12:03,693 --> 00:12:05,458
The goldfish just disappeared!

176
00:12:26,593 --> 00:12:31,358
I was hiding in the fish tank the whole
time and used this mirror for camouflage!

177
00:12:31,613 --> 00:12:35,230
A kid could've figured out my
plan and you totally fell for it!

178
00:12:35,313 --> 00:12:38,090
I was worried that something
so simple wasn't gonna work,

179
00:12:38,173 --> 00:12:41,585
but lucky for me, you're just
as stupid as you are creepy!

180
00:12:43,813 --> 00:12:46,550
Doesn't matter if Cherry is
stuck in his two-year-old form,

181
00:12:46,633 --> 00:12:48,610
he can still skewer your face, dumbass!

182
00:12:48,693 --> 00:12:49,553
Ha ha ha!

183
00:12:55,953 --> 00:12:56,783
Yaaah!

184
00:12:56,866 --> 00:12:57,696
Bad boy!

185
00:12:57,813 --> 00:12:59,733
Bad boy! Hey!

186
00:12:59,953 --> 00:13:01,306
Get your ass back here!

187
00:13:01,953 --> 00:13:02,783
Hey, wait!

188
00:13:02,866 --> 00:13:06,104
Until you break your stand
spell, I'm gonna keep attacking!

189
00:13:07,153 --> 00:13:09,153
Bad boy! Bad boy!

190
00:13:09,413 --> 00:13:11,113
You're such a bad boy!

191
00:13:12,313 --> 00:13:15,073
Evolve, that jerk dropped out the window!

192
00:13:18,953 --> 00:13:20,013
Bad boy!

193
00:13:20,373 --> 00:13:22,033
What a horrible boy!

194
00:13:27,053 --> 00:13:27,883
Jotaro!

195
00:13:28,433 --> 00:13:29,263
Crap!

196
00:13:29,353 --> 00:13:31,413
If he's here, then I'm done for!

197
00:13:32,073 --> 00:13:34,853
How'd he find us? Hmm.

198
00:13:43,513 --> 00:13:46,278
Someone falling from a
window covered in blood.

199
00:13:46,453 --> 00:13:48,159
You don't see that every day.

200
00:13:48,733 --> 00:13:49,693
Stay calm.

201
00:13:49,913 --> 00:13:50,833
Stay calm.

202
00:13:51,073 --> 00:13:54,426
At times like this, the winner
is the one who stays calm.

203
00:13:54,773 --> 00:13:56,420
Just think about it, Alessi.

204
00:13:56,753 --> 00:13:59,510
Jotaro must be looking for the
adult version of Polnareff.

205
00:13:59,593 --> 00:14:01,073
He has no clue who I am.

206
00:14:01,673 --> 00:14:03,213
I'll do what I always do.

207
00:14:03,353 --> 00:14:04,950
Play dumb until the last minute.

208
00:14:05,033 --> 00:14:07,445
Then attack him when he least expects it.

209
00:14:10,973 --> 00:14:11,803
Oh, no!

210
00:14:12,073 --> 00:14:16,070
My boss is going to be so very
angry with me when he finds out!

211
00:14:16,153 --> 00:14:20,506
There I was, cleaning the window, and
I suddenly slipped and fell through!

212
00:14:20,733 --> 00:14:22,333
What am I going to do?

213
00:14:22,573 --> 00:14:23,867
What am I going to do?

214
00:14:24,133 --> 00:14:25,753
I am in so much trouble!

215
00:14:25,853 --> 00:14:28,794
Hold it right there, you
frizzy-haired freak show!

216
00:14:29,813 --> 00:14:30,673
Hey, mister!

217
00:14:32,053 --> 00:14:33,465
What was his name again?

218
00:14:33,593 --> 00:14:34,833
Come on, what was it?

219
00:14:36,753 --> 00:14:37,733
Now's my chance!

220
00:14:37,973 --> 00:14:41,130
I was waiting for Polnareff to
poke his annoying little head out!

221
00:14:41,213 --> 00:14:42,773
Getcha now, Jotaro!

222
00:14:43,953 --> 00:14:45,894
Mister, watch out for his shadow!

223
00:14:47,613 --> 00:14:48,533
I did it!

224
00:14:48,693 --> 00:14:49,634
I really did it!

225
00:14:49,733 --> 00:14:51,792
I managed to touch Jojuro's shadow!

226
00:14:52,453 --> 00:14:53,293
Mr. No!

227
00:14:56,133 --> 00:15:00,251
So, Jojuro, how does it feel to be
placed under the spell of my stand?

228
00:15:03,853 --> 00:15:04,813
This feeling...

229
00:15:05,953 --> 00:15:06,913
This is...

230
00:15:07,533 --> 00:15:08,513
This is bad!

231
00:15:08,713 --> 00:15:11,066
He's turning into a kid just like I did!

232
00:15:11,233 --> 00:15:12,353
Oh, Jojuro!

233
00:15:12,813 --> 00:15:16,470
I heard through the grapevine that you've
only recently developed your stand,

234
00:15:16,553 --> 00:15:17,383
Star Platinum.

235
00:15:17,633 --> 00:15:22,398
And that means you didn't have the ability
to use your stand when you were a kid.

236
00:15:22,553 --> 00:15:24,612
So now you're nothing but ordinary.

237
00:15:29,333 --> 00:15:32,353
Oh no, he's been turned into a little boy.

238
00:15:32,593 --> 00:15:36,005
It looks like he can't be any
older than a seven-year-old.

239
00:15:37,373 --> 00:15:38,608
Guess I'm the winner.

240
00:15:38,793 --> 00:15:41,810
Hope you're watching, Master Dio,
because I'm about to kill Jojaro.

241
00:15:41,893 --> 00:15:45,450
You'd better give me a good reward
for everything I've come through.

242
00:15:45,533 --> 00:15:48,113
Now, Jujuru, it's time to die!

243
00:15:50,793 --> 00:15:52,253
Oh, what a hit!

244
00:15:52,453 --> 00:15:55,100
He decked him using only
his little kid fist!

245
00:15:57,633 --> 00:15:58,893
Oh, good grief.

246
00:15:59,293 --> 00:16:01,999
Don't underestimate me
just because I'm a kid.

247
00:16:11,893 --> 00:16:12,723
Shut up!

248
00:16:16,073 --> 00:16:16,903
What?

249
00:16:16,986 --> 00:16:20,930
You're seriously telling me that Jocharo
could kick ass even as a little kid?

250
00:16:21,013 --> 00:16:25,153
I knew he was tough, but he was
that strong as a kid? Bites!

251
00:16:49,073 --> 00:16:51,893
You got off easy, friend,
but I can fix that.

252
00:17:06,413 --> 00:17:07,243
Manipa!

253
00:17:07,326 --> 00:17:08,513
Stand, set,

254
00:17:08,893 --> 00:17:12,473
God of Chaos and Storms,
Alessi, 38 years old,

255
00:17:12,673 --> 00:17:14,908
single, and an unfortunate projectile,

256
00:17:15,113 --> 00:17:16,313
out of commission!

257
00:17:32,493 --> 00:17:34,193
Was all of that a dream?

258
00:17:40,953 --> 00:17:42,910
This earring belongs to that boy.

259
00:17:42,993 --> 00:17:45,093
So it really did happen.

260
00:17:45,873 --> 00:17:47,170
I don't know why!

261
00:17:47,253 --> 00:17:48,370
But for some reason!

262
00:17:48,453 --> 00:17:49,850
I couldn't move my body.

263
00:17:49,933 --> 00:17:51,290
That's right.

264
00:17:51,373 --> 00:17:53,510
I may not have been able to move!

265
00:17:53,593 --> 00:17:54,990
But I remember everything.

266
00:17:55,073 --> 00:17:57,330
That sweet little boy.

267
00:17:57,413 --> 00:17:59,230
Devoted himself to protecting me.

268
00:17:59,313 --> 00:18:00,870
And risked his life.

269
00:18:00,953 --> 00:18:02,490
By fighting against a grown man.

270
00:18:02,573 --> 00:18:05,173
He had such a brave and heroic heart.

271
00:18:05,813 --> 00:18:07,342
Oh, where did that boy go?

272
00:18:07,933 --> 00:18:08,763
Where?

273
00:18:08,933 --> 00:18:11,168
Where did my little knight run off to?

274
00:18:12,353 --> 00:18:13,533
Where did you go?

275
00:18:13,793 --> 00:18:14,773
Where are you?

276
00:18:17,813 --> 00:18:20,453
I've never met such an
amazing woman before.

277
00:18:21,153 --> 00:18:22,893
So kind. So genuine.

278
00:18:23,893 --> 00:18:27,658
That was a close one, but thankfully
I'm back to my normal self.

279
00:18:28,113 --> 00:18:29,833
I wonder if she's okay.

280
00:18:38,213 --> 00:18:39,370
I hate to bother you,

281
00:18:39,453 --> 00:18:41,510
but you didn't happen
to see a sweet little

282
00:18:41,593 --> 00:18:43,310
boy leave my house in
something of a hurry,

283
00:18:43,393 --> 00:18:44,223
did you?

284
00:18:44,873 --> 00:18:46,050
He has silver hair.

285
00:18:46,133 --> 00:18:49,015
Come to think of it, it
looks exactly like yours.

286
00:18:57,693 --> 00:19:00,987
Pardon me for asking, but
have the two of us met before?

287
00:19:05,993 --> 00:19:08,111
No, I didn't see a kid come through.

288
00:19:08,373 --> 00:19:09,902
Sorry I couldn't help you.

289
00:19:10,373 --> 00:19:11,373
Let's go, Jotaro.

290
00:19:14,133 --> 00:19:15,733
Come on, hurry up!

291
00:19:17,213 --> 00:19:18,053
Please wait!

292
00:19:18,833 --> 00:19:20,010
Could you be...

293
00:19:20,093 --> 00:19:22,533
That earring you're wearing...

294
00:19:23,613 --> 00:19:25,753
The two of us have never met before.

295
00:19:26,413 --> 00:19:27,613
It's not possible.

296
00:19:28,193 --> 00:19:29,958
My friend and I are travelers.

297
00:19:30,753 --> 00:19:34,459
So if you'll excuse us, there's
another town we need to get to.

298
00:19:35,173 --> 00:19:36,291
We'll be going now.

299
00:19:41,393 --> 00:19:43,093
It was only a dream.

300
00:19:43,773 --> 00:19:44,733
Too bad.

301
00:19:51,933 --> 00:19:54,213
Not a single word from you, Jotaro.

302
00:19:54,533 --> 00:19:55,945
I don't want to hear it.

303
00:20:02,273 --> 00:20:03,103
No!

304
00:20:03,186 --> 00:20:05,293
Joe Dario and Polnareff!

305
00:20:05,753 --> 00:20:08,390
Where in the world have
you two slackers been?

306
00:20:08,473 --> 00:20:09,453
Ah, Mr.

307
00:20:09,593 --> 00:20:10,753
Joestar and Avdol.

308
00:20:11,693 --> 00:20:15,670
How many times have I told the two of
you not to go wandering off on your own?

309
00:20:15,753 --> 00:20:17,350
Oh, you're in a position to talk.

310
00:20:17,433 --> 00:20:19,551
You're the one who just disappeared.

311
00:20:20,133 --> 00:20:20,963
Now, now.

312
00:20:21,173 --> 00:20:25,233
Why don't we focus on getting
something to eat? Huh? Hey Iggy!

313
00:20:25,413 --> 00:20:27,884
Where the hell have you been all day long?

314
00:20:40,013 --> 00:20:41,425
Can I take that for you?

315
00:20:44,693 --> 00:20:46,046
Yeah, thanks a million.

316
00:20:48,273 --> 00:20:51,390
It's about time, we're finally
getting a bit of relief.

317
00:20:51,473 --> 00:20:55,532
It was quite the late breakfast,
but I suppose it couldn't be helped.

318
00:20:56,253 --> 00:20:58,490
Yeah, since we've almost made it to Cairo,

319
00:20:58,573 --> 00:21:01,926
I think it's time we figured
out where Dio is hiding out.

320
00:21:03,193 --> 00:21:08,090
oh we're doing this will it
appear I'm not sure but given that

321
00:21:08,173 --> 00:21:12,793
we're so close the result should be
more precise all right here we go

322
00:21:20,133 --> 00:21:24,833
excuse me sir is there a problem over
here everything's fine mind your own

323
00:21:25,413 --> 00:21:26,493
Uh, yes.

324
00:21:30,413 --> 00:21:33,673
Old man, tell us, what is it?

325
00:21:34,033 --> 00:21:35,373
Just a little longer.

326
00:21:35,833 --> 00:21:37,373
I see something.

327
00:21:37,733 --> 00:21:39,453
It's getting clearer.

328
00:21:41,353 --> 00:21:42,893
Take a good look!

329
00:21:45,833 --> 00:21:46,910
There you have it, gentlemen!

330
00:21:46,993 --> 00:21:48,287
Our final destination!

331
00:22:28,333 --> 00:22:29,163
Thank you.

332
00:23:03,333 --> 00:23:04,163
Thank you.

333
00:23:28,213 --> 00:23:29,930
You're the one who fell for the scam.

334
00:23:30,013 --> 00:23:31,830
I've had just about enough of your games.

335
00:23:31,913 --> 00:23:33,710
Gambling is just like relationships.

336
00:23:33,793 --> 00:23:35,170
The one who cries loses.

337
00:23:35,253 --> 00:23:38,310
If he does anything that seems
suspicious, you can go home.

338
00:23:38,393 --> 00:23:40,450
If you're scared, exactly right.

339
00:23:40,533 --> 00:23:42,573
I'm going to bet my soul. Good?
